   "reference": {
    "title": "WHO 5th phaeochromocytoma / paraganglioma & SDHB screening",
    "intro": "All phaeochromocytomas and paragangliomas are regarded as having metastatic potential (the terms 'benign' and 'malignant' are no longer used). SDHB immunohistochemistry is strongly recommended on all PPGLs to screen for hereditary SDHx mutations.",
    "note": "Photomicrographs are from Wikimedia Commons under open Creative Commons licences. ExpertPath pages open with your own ExpertPath login; the app holds none of their images.",
    "groups": [
     {
      "heading": "Diagnostic phenotype, SDHB & risk scores",
      "points": [
       "Classic Zellballen (nested) architecture of polygonal basophilic/amphophilic chief cells surrounded by S100/SOX10-positive sustentacular cells; positive for chromogranin A, synaptophysin, INSM1, GATA3 and tyrosine hydroxylase; negative for keratins.",
       "Loss of granular cytoplasmic SDHB staining indicates an underlying SDHx (SDHA/B/C/D) mutation and high metastatic risk — recommend clinical genetics referral.",
       "PASS (>= 4) and GAPP (0–2 well, 3–6 moderately, 7–10 poorly differentiated) may be recorded as ancillary risk tools alongside Ki-67 % and mitotic count per 2 mm2."
      ],
      "links": [
       {
        "label": "ExpertPath: Pheochromocytoma and Paraganglioma",
        "url": "https://app.expertpath.com/"
       }
      ],
      "images": [
